Text:
fearlessMessage is a program that sends one Message to the single manager, and prints the Answer of the single manager on the standard output of fearlessMessage.
The single manager is 'reachable at Port' when the ManagerFolder at the 'manager path' holds the LockFile "single_manager_at_" Port ".lock", and a process holds the lock of that LockFile.
The single manager is 'not reachable' when no Port makes the single manager reachable at that Port.
The 'name' of a folder is ProjectName when ProjectName ".fearless" is the only file at top level in that folder ending with ".fearless".

Grammar:
Message ::= "EditMetadata " Base16                                     \
          | "EditMetadata " Info                                       \
          | "Register " Base16                                         \
          | "Forget " Target                                           \
          | "Forget " Base16                                           \
          | "Kind " Target " " Kind                                    \
          | "Mount " Target " " TypeName " " Target'                   \
          | "Unmount " Target " " TypeName                             \
          | "Attenuate " Target " " TypeName " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen  \
          | "SelectMains " Target " " TypeName1 " ".." " TypeNamen             \
          | "Quit"
Target ::= "Name(" ProjectName ")" | "Full(" ProjectName " " Base16 ")"
Base16 ::= "Base16:" ([0-9A-F][0-9A-F])+
Answer ::= "Applied\n" | "Refused\n" Error
Error ::= ...
AnyText ::= any sequence of characters

Well formedness:
in Base16: Base16 encodes a valid OS FS path

Define fearlessMessage$send(Message,Port):
A action fearlessMessage connects to Port on the loopback address, and sends Message on the connection
B action fearlessMessage prints on the standard output of fearlessMessage the text arriving on the connection, as the text arrives
C fact The connection is closed.
D action fearlessMessage ends

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with exactly one argument.
B fact The argument is Message.
C fact The single manager is reachable at Port.
D action fearlessMessage$send(Message,Port)

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with exactly one argument.
B fact The argument is Message.
C fact The single manager is not reachable.
D action fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager, and waits until the single manager is reachable or one minute has passed
E after The single manager is reachable at Port.
F action fearlessMessage$send(Message,Port)

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with exactly one argument.
B fact The argument is Message.
C fact The single manager is not reachable.
D action fearlessMessage runs fearlessManager, and waits until the single manager is reachable or one minute has passed
E after The single manager is not reachable.
F action fearlessMessage prints internalErrorManagerNotStarted() on the standard error of fearlessMessage, and ends

Story:
A event fearlessMessage is called with the arguments AnyText1 .. AnyTextn.
B fact n is not 1, or AnyText1 is not of form Message.
C action fearlessMessage prints messageErrorArgumentsAreNotOneMessage(AnyText1 .. AnyTextn) on the standard error of fearlessMessage, and ends

Implementation notes:
The design gives no syntax for a call of fearlessMessage: a program gets its arguments already cut, with no trace of how the caller wrote them. Each shell has its own rules to cut the text of a call into arguments, and a program can start fearlessMessage with a list of arguments and no shell.
A shell cuts at each space that is outside a quotation, and most Messages hold a space: a caller in a shell uses a quotation of that shell, as in fearlessMessage "Register Base16:432F61".
A Message made only of Base16, ProjectName, TypeName and Kind arrives unchanged between double quotes from sh, bash, zsh, cmd.exe and PowerShell.
A Message that holds a TaggedText of form "Str:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn or "UStr:" EscapedChar1 .. EscapedCharn can hold characters with a meaning inside the double quotes of some shell, such as the double quote, "$", "\\", "`" and "%": a shell can remove or replace those characters, and the argument is then another text, which can be another Message. A caller in a shell sends such a Message as "EditMetadata " Base16.
fearlessMessage sends Message on the connection as the argument holds it, and fearlessManager$delegate returns a Message to fearlessManager.queue with no shell in between: fearlessManager handles a Message of form "EditMetadata " Info with any Info.
